// 01 · Drift — the bare agent loop, and the price of being alive.
//
// The simplest living scene: a handful of WANDERERS and no food. Each runs the
// invariant loop (perceive → decide → act, SIM Law 2) and pays the allometric
// COST LAW every second — maintenance (∝ body size) + locomotion (∝ size · speed).
// With nothing to eat, a reserve can only fall: the population drifts, thins, and
// winks out. Reproduction is off (`reproduction_threshold: 0`), so this is
// mortality in isolation — the metabolic floor every later scenario must beat by
// finding energy (sunlight, then prey).
//
// Watch: the energy bars drain; the arena falls quiet within ~30 s. A tight arena,
// because there is nothing to spread out for.
(
    tick_hz: 64.0,
    arena_half_extent: 220.0,
    archetypes: [
        (
            name: "Wanderer",
            color: (0.55, 0.75, 1.0),
            count: 40,
            radius: 8.0,
            reserve_max: 100.0,
            genotype: (
                max_speed: 120.0,
                agility: 0.12,
                vision_range: 90.0,
                vision_fov_deg: 120.0,
                reproduction_threshold: 0.0, // no reproduction — pure mortality
                mutation_rate: 0.0,
                vision_rays: 5.0,
            ),
            brain: Wander(turn_rate: 0.25),
            mutable: (),
        ),
    ],
    seed: 1,
)
